  "**random** — for games, simulations and picking things:\n\n- `random.randint(1, 6)` — a whole number from 1 to 6 (**both included**).\n- `random.choice(list)` — one random item.\n- `random.shuffle(list)` — mixes a list in place.\n- `random.random()` — a float between 0 and 1.\n- `random.seed(42)` — makes the \"random\" results repeatable (great for testing).\n\n**math** — beyond basic operators:\n\n- `math.sqrt(x)`, `math.pi`, `math.floor(x)`, `math.ceil(x)`\n- `math.pow(x, y)`, `math.gcd(a, b)`, `math.factorial(n)`\n- `math.sin`, `math.cos` (angles in radians)",
  "**random** — oʻyinlar, simulyatsiyalar va tanlash uchun:\n\n- `random.randint(1, 6)` — 1 dan 6 gacha butun son (**ikkala chegara ham kiradi**).\n- `random.choice(list)` — bitta tasodifiy element.\n- `random.shuffle(list)` — roʻyxatni oʻz joyida aralashtiradi.\n- `random.random()` — 0 va 1 orasidagi oʻnli son.\n- `random.seed(42)` — “tasodifiy” natijalarni takrorlanadigan qiladi (test uchun juda qulay).\n\n**math** — oddiy operatorlardan tashqari:\n\n- `math.sqrt(x)`, `math.pi`, `math.floor(x)`, `math.ceil(x)`\n- `math.pow(x, y)`, `math.gcd(a, b)`, `math.factorial(n)`\n- `math.sin`, `math.cos` (burchaklar radianda)",
